<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23295" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infrēnis</span></b> , e, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infrēnus</span></b> , a,
		um (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infraen-</span></b> ),
			adj.
		2. in - frenum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>without a bridle</i>, <i>unbridled</i> (<b>poet.</b> and post-class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infrenis equus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 10, 750</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Numidae infreni,</span>”
				<i>on unbridled horses</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 41</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>untamed</i>, <i>unchecked</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infreno volitare cursu, Col. poët. 10,
					215: lingua infrenis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 1, 15, 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infrenus manat de vulnere sanguis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ser. Samm. 43, 804</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
